<!-- ================= WORKSHOPS ================= -->
<div class="view" data-view="workshops" id="workshops" hidden>
  <section class="phead ctr"><div class="wrap"><div class="panel mist with-art">
    <svg class="phead-art" viewBox="0 0 320 300" aria-hidden="true"><g transform="translate(36 20) rotate(-12 40 125)"><use href="#t-phillips" width="80" height="250"/></g><g transform="translate(116 6)"><use href="#t-tape" width="90" height="270"/></g><g transform="translate(210 22) rotate(12 40 125)"><use href="#t-flat" width="80" height="250"/></g></svg>
    <h1 class="h-xl" tabindex="-1" data-focus>Hands-on sessions, led in person</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="color:#46504A">Each workshop covers one topic with hands-on practice. Here’s how we plan to run them once we launch. Nothing is running or booking yet.</p>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="sec tight"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="h-lg">Planned prices</h2><p class="lede">Book us for a workshop, or run the activities yourself with a monthly plan. These are planned prices, and nothing is booking yet.</p></div>
    <div class="plans">
    <div class="pc" id="plan-live">
      <div class="pc-top"><span class="chip soon">Planned</span><h3>In person</h3><p>We come to you with the supplies. Up to 30 students per session.</p></div>
      <div class="pc-cols">
        <div class="pc-col"><h4>50-minute workshop</h4><p class="price">$200 <small>/ session</small></p><p>One topic, hands-on. Fits in a class period or after school.</p></div>
        <div class="pc-col"><h4>90-minute workshop</h4><p class="price">$300 <small>/ session</small></p><p>More hands-on time, or two topics in one session.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pc-row"><h4>Series or family day</h4><p>Several topics over a few weeks, or a day where students and families learn together. Priced per session.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pc mo" id="plan-monthly">
      <div class="pc-top"><span class="chip soon">Planned</span><h3>Monthly, online</h3><p>New activities and printable guides every month. You run them with your students, on your schedule.</p></div>
      <div class="pc-cols">
        <div class="pc-col"><h4>Teacher plan</h4><p class="price">$9.99 <small>/ month</small></p><p>For teachers, volunteers and community group leaders. Show proof, like a school ID or a letter from your group, and tell us why this rate fits you.</p></div>
        <div class="pc-col"><h4>Team plan</h4><p class="price">$19.99 <small>/ month</small></p><p>One plan you share with up to two other teachers or staff at your school or group. About $6.66 each.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pc-row"><h4>Who goes first</h4><p>Schools and groups that serve low-income families get the first spots.</p></div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="wrap"><div class="panel sand">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="h-lg">Matched to their age</h2><p class="lede" style="color:#46504A">Same topics, adjusted to what each age can safely do.</p></div>
    <div class="agewrap">
      <div class="modes fit" role="tablist" aria-label="Age groups" id="ageTabs">
        <button class="mode" type="button" role="tab" id="agt-1" aria-controls="agp-1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">Grades 3 to 5</button>
        <button class="mode" type="button" role="tab" id="agt-2" aria-controls="agp-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Grades 6 to 8</button>
        <button class="mode" type="button" role="tab" id="agt-3" aria-controls="agp-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Older students</button>
      </div>
      <div class="agep">
        <article class="tier on" role="tabpanel" id="agp-1" aria-labelledby="agt-1"><h3>Elementary, grades 3 to 5</h3><p>Short, simple tasks with lots of moving around.</p><ul><li>Name tools and what they’re for</li><li>Spot a “you won a prize” message</li><li>Practice asking for help, out loud</li></ul></article>
        <article class="tier" role="tabpanel" id="agp-2" aria-labelledby="agt-2"><h3>Middle school, grades 6 to 8</h3><p>More on their own, and more real-life decisions.</p><ul><li>Tighten a screw, hang something level</li><li>Lock down an account</li><li>Plan and track a weekend budget</li></ul></article>
        <article class="tier" role="tabpanel" id="agp-3" aria-labelledby="agt-3"><span class="chip soon" style="justify-self:start">Preview</span><h3>Older students</h3><p>Planned for later, after we launch for grades 3 to 8.</p><ul><li>Vehicle basics with an adult</li><li>Budgeting a first paycheck</li><li>Workplace communication</li></ul></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div></section>

